.TH CMDREF 7 "2026-04-05" "Your Name" "Personal Command Reference"
.SH NAME
cmdref \- a collection of useful bash commands

.SH SYNOPSIS
(no executable; this is a reference document)

.SH DESCRIPTION
This manual page stores bash commands I find or invent.

.SH COMMANDS
.SS Exclude .tree and .png files
.nf
find . -maxdepth 1 -type f ! -name "*.tree" ! -name "*.png" -printf "%f\\n"
.fi
Explanation: \fB-maxdepth 1\fR stays in current directory, \fB-printf "%f"\fR strips './'

.SS All\-uppercase filenames (POSIX)
.nf
( LC_ALL=C; for f in *; do [ -f "$f" ] && case $f in *[!A-Z]*) ;; *) printf '%s\\n' "$f";; esac; done )
.fi
Uses \fBcase\fR to reject any non\-A\-Z character.

.SH SEE ALSO
bash(1), find(1), man(7)

